{
  "content": "<h1><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ExpenseClaimPayers\">Expense Claim Payers</span></h1><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"And Business ExpenseClaim ExpenseClaimPayers ExpenseClaimsPayer Expenses To ToDate\"><em>Expense claim payers</em> are individuals or entities who pay for business expenses using their own funds and need to be reimbursed.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Business Employee Employees Expense_claims ExpenseClaim ExpenseClaims Expenses Is On To ToDate\">Use this feature to maintain a list of people who can submit expense claims to your business, such as employees, contractors, or business owners who pay for business expenses personally.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Add ExpenseClaim ExpenseClaimsPayer NewExpenseClaim NewExpenseClaimPayer On To ToDate\">To add a new expense claim payer, click the <strong>New Expense Claim Payer</strong> button.</p><div class=\"flex pointer-events-none space-x-6 rtl:space-x-reverse items-center\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block ltr:pr-8 rtl:pl-8\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-200 ltr:pl-8 rtl:pr-8\"><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"border-y ltr:border-l rtl:border-r border-neutral-300 bg-white p-4 flex gap-2 items-center\"><i class=\"fas fa-cog text-neutral-400\"></i><span class=\"font-semibold text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Settings\">Settings</span></span></div><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div></div></div><span class=\"rtl:hidden\"><i class=\"fas fa-circle-chevron-right text-lg text-neutral-300\"></i></span><span class=\"ltr:hidden\"><i class=\"fas fa-circle-chevron-left text-lg text-neutral-300\"></i></span><div class=\"border rounded inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"basis-72 flex items-center gap-2 p-4\"><i class=\"text-xl text-neutral-400 fas fa-fw fa-user-tie\"></i><span class=\"text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"ExpenseClaimPayers\">Expense Claim Payers</span></span></div></div></div>",
